Command:
  rtk env GOMAXPROCS=2 go test -p 2 ./internal/tools -run '^(TestStreamingBashDrainsPastMaxOutput|TestStreamingBashDrainsConcurrentStdoutStderr|TestStreamingBashLongLineReportsScannerErrorAndDrains|TestStreamingBashCancellationWaitsForReaders)$' -count=1 -timeout 12s -v
Exit code: 1

Observed against the unmodified implementation:

- `TestStreamingBashDrainsPastMaxOutput` failed because the finite 200,000-byte
  Bash builtin timed out at 1.2 seconds with `context deadline exceeded`.
- `TestStreamingBashDrainsConcurrentStdoutStderr` failed at the tool timeout
  while both finite streams were larger than the OS pipe buffer.
- `TestStreamingBashLongLineReportsScannerErrorAndDrains` exposed the same
  timeout when a 2,000,000-byte no-newline output token exceeded Scanner's 1 MiB
  limit; the old helper ignored `Scanner.Err()` and stopped draining.
- `TestStreamingBashCancellationWaitsForReaders` passed before the fix. It is a
  lifecycle guard for the post-fix active-drain path, not evidence of the bug.

The first two failures reproduce the reported pipe-backpressure defect. The
long-line case confirms the separate early-stop path caused by an ignored
scanner error. No command starts a child process.
